-- title:
--   Level-one supersingular node pairs are indexed by j-invariants
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$, and let $S_0 \subseteq k$ be a finite set whose elements are exactly the members of `ssJSet q k`, i.e. those $j \in k$ such that every Weierstrass curve $W$ over $k$ which is elliptic and has $W.j = j$ has no nonzero point $P$ with $q \cdot P = 0$. The assertion is the existence of a finite set $W$ of places of the level-one modular function field `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` — the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $k((t))$ over $k$ generated by the $q$-expansions `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k 1`, a place being a valuation subring containing the image of $k$, distinct from the whole field and a principal ideal ring — with two properties: membership in $W$ is equivalent to membership in `ssPlaces q 1 k`, the set of places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w(\,\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,k\,1\,) \in$ `ssJSet q k`; and `nodePairsOfPlaces (arithFrobC q k 1) W`, the image of $W$ under the pairing embedding attached to the semilinear automorphism `arithFrobC q k 1` induced by the coefficientwise Frobenius $x \mapsto x^q$ of $k$, coincides with `nodePairsOf q S₀`, the image of $S_0$ under the embedding `frobNodePairEmb q`.
--
--   This identifies, at level one, the node pairs of the special fibre indexed by supersingular places of the modular function field with those indexed directly by supersingular $j$-invariants, the two bookkeeping devices used for the crossings in characteristic $q$. It is used in the construction of level-one prolongation tuples and models and in the computation of the order of the component group attached to the node pairs.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_nodePairsOfPlaces_arithFrobC_eq_nodePairsOf.lean

